//< Fewer type arguments than the declaration has are rejected
//<
//< A type variable left unsubstituted goes straight into the generated C and the C compiler says
//< `unknown type name 'U'` ("Failing fast through an exception or an ICE" in ksplc/docs/DESIGN.md).
// EXPECT: too few type arguments for generic 'W': it declares 2, but 1 given
struct W<|T, U|>
  a: T
  b: U
fn main()
  _x: W<|I32|>
